r" rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.55 (&#x02212;35.70 to 62.80)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p</italic> = 0.2193</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p</italic> = 0.5894</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Length of all roadways within 200 m of the home (km)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">256.15<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn9-ehp-116-1423">b</xref> (52.52 to 459.78)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">77.60 (0.51 to 154.68)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p</italic> = 0.0139</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p</italic> = 0.0485</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn8-ehp-116-1423"><label>a</label><p>&#x003b2; is the regression coefficient for the natural logarithm of eNO multiplied by 1,000.</p></fn><fn id="tfn9-ehp-116-1423"><label>b</label><p>This is equivalent to a 29.2% (95% CI, 5.4 to 58.4) increase in eNO for a 1-km increase in roadway.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>